00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:43.340
They said, we are Jews, religious,

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:46.340
never the word religion does not appear

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:49.179
in the vocabulary of the Sephardim.

00:15:49.179 --> 00:15:55.859
They said, we are members of the Jewish nation,

00:15:55.859 --> 00:15:58.619
the Jewish nation.

00:15:58.619 --> 00:16:04.179
They consider themselves as a different political entity,

00:16:04.179 --> 00:16:09.979
not under the jurisdiction of the local country.

00:16:09.979 --> 00:16:15.219
Whether we were in Portugal, whether we were in Amsterdam,

00:16:15.219 --> 00:16:18.979
whether we were in Livorno, in Thessaloniki, or Damascus,

00:16:18.979 --> 00:16:23.099
or Halab, or Egypt, the Jew was not

00:16:23.099 --> 00:16:31.179
under the legal jurisdiction of the political establishment.

00:16:31.179 --> 00:16:33.380
They had autonomy.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.539
They were an autonomous nation, yes?

00:16:36.539 --> 00:16:40.340
To the point that it was considered literally

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:43.299
like a foreign nation, all right?

00:16:43.299 --> 00:16:46.940
Napoleon is the first one who offered the Jew the following.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:52.940
He says, you may become now a citizen.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:55.219
You may become a citizen.

00:16:55.219 --> 00:16:58.260
But in order to become a citizen,

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:04.260
you have to forfeit your claim to be a nation.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:07.020
You have to be a religion.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:09.180
France will have many religions.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.540
Of course, the religion of the state is Catholic.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:14.260
But people from other religions also,

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:17.939
they will have full participation

00:17:17.939 --> 00:17:19.420
in the life of the state.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:26.099
So now, Napoleon offered the Jew for the first time

00:17:26.099 --> 00:17:32.579
the possibility of joining and becoming full citizen.

00:17:32.619 --> 00:17:34.699
But there was a catch.

00:17:34.699 --> 00:17:37.859
The catch is, you're no longer a nation.

00:17:37.859 --> 00:17:42.020
You're only a religion, all right?

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:45.739
Moses Mendelssohn, the reform, grabbed it.

00:17:45.739 --> 00:17:48.260
What was the whole theory of the reform?

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:51.380
And the purpose of my idea is not to criticize anybody,

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.060
but just to try to understand.

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:57.260
Judaism is a religion.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:00.939
We have no political claims.

00:18:00.939 --> 00:18:05.180
We are politically, we are like any other members

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:08.780
of the German Republic.

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:09.339
Yes?

00:18:09.339 --> 00:18:10.660
We have a different religion.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.140
There's some people are Protestant.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.540
Some are Catholic.

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.380
Some are Jews.

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:16.699
But we do not have.

00:18:16.699 --> 00:18:20.180
That's why the whole motto of the reform movement

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:27.660
is Berlin is our Jerusalem, and Germany is our Israel.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:31.739
And therefore, he wrote a very famous book, Moses Mendelssohn,

00:18:31.739 --> 00:18:34.619
called Jerusalem, in which Jerusalem becomes

00:18:34.619 --> 00:18:36.300
only an ideology.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:42.260
It is no longer a local geography.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:45.699
And therefore, the Mashiah, if there will be a Mashiah,

00:18:45.699 --> 00:18:50.020
it is not going to be a Mashiah like Rambam,

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.859
but it's going to be a Mashiah like Shabbat HaSevi.

00:18:53.859 --> 00:18:58.739
Ideology, this, ethics, all this type of things.

00:18:58.739 --> 00:19:02.939
In a very interesting way, just let me tell you a parenthesis.

00:19:02.939 --> 00:19:05.500
For some of you, I'm interested in laws,

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.979
because I think law is always, it tells you the past of a nation.

00:19:08.979 --> 00:19:14.180
The Sanhedrin was conveyed by Napoleon 1806.

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.459
Yes?

00:19:15.459 --> 00:19:17.420
Two things very important about the Sanhedrin.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.780
I'll tell you later, I'm going to call the details of the Sanhedrin

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:20.900
a very interesting thing.

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:26.900
Number one, the purpose of the Sanhedrin

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:31.859
was to abrogate the question of the Jewish nation.

00:19:31.859 --> 00:19:35.900
The great Sepharadi, the Sepharadi Hagamim refused to come there.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.099
Rabbi Shemael HaKohen, and also all these Hagamim

00:19:38.099 --> 00:19:39.939
refused to attend the Sanhedrin.

00:19:39.939 --> 00:19:41.300
Yes?

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.579
The Ashkenaz Rabbis did attend, and this

00:19:43.579 --> 00:19:47.579
is where the first rift between Sephardim and Ashkenaz come.

00:19:47.579 --> 00:19:50.020
The people who attended, the Sephardim

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:56.380
who attended the Sanhedrin were not rabbis, were only laymen.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:59.739
The Hagamim, and there's a reason why.

00:19:59.739 --> 00:20:04.979
Because once that you forfeit your national dimension,

00:20:04.979 --> 00:20:07.739
then you no longer have a claim for Israel.

00:20:07.739 --> 00:20:09.300
There's no longer Galut.

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:11.859
There is no purpose of the Mashiah.

00:20:11.859 --> 00:20:17.339
A Danish or a Swede cannot have a Mashiah,

00:20:17.339 --> 00:20:23.140
because already has Sweden or Denmark or Norway or wherever it is.

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:28.739
In the same way, if you are German or you are French,

00:20:28.739 --> 00:20:30.260
then what's the purpose of the Mashiah?

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.020
For another land?

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:33.739
But you have already a land.

00:20:33.739 --> 00:20:35.660
This is your land.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:36.780
You cannot be in Galut.

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:41.780
How could you be in Galut if you are a full citizen of whatever

00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:43.780
country you happen to be?

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:47.939
So the Sepharadi Hagamim deliberately,

00:20:47.939 --> 00:20:52.020
they abstained from joining to go into the Sanhedrin.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.819
Just now a question of law, which is an interesting thing.

00:20:54.819 --> 00:20:55.459
Listen to this.

00:20:55.459 --> 00:20:58.900
Interesting thing for a point of law.

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:05.660
There were debts incurred by members of the Sepharadi community in France

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:06.859
before the Sanhedrin.

00:21:06.859 --> 00:21:12.020
I don't know, the Knesset owed 500 francs to Mr. So-and-so,

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:16.500
because they painted the Knesset.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:21.140
The Sanhedrin proclaims no longer a Jewish nation.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.979
We have the records of this.

00:21:23.979 --> 00:21:25.780
The records exist.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:30.300
Again, the person says, well, you owe me $500 from the Knesset.

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:32.339
The Knesset refused to pay.

00:21:32.339 --> 00:21:33.540
Why?

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.859
You, this law was with the Jewish nation.

00:21:36.859 --> 00:21:39.300
The Jewish nation no longer exists.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:42.300
It was taken to court.

00:21:42.300 --> 00:21:44.819
And the court was in favor of the Jewish community.

00:21:44.819 --> 00:21:48.260
There is no longer a Jewish nation.

00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:50.060
And that is the policy of France.

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:53.500
Everything for the individual Jew, nothing for the Jewish community

00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:57.060
as an entity.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:00.260
So for the individual Jew, yes.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.140
For the community as such, not.

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:04.780
So just I wanted you to understand.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:08.939
Shabbatai Sevin, a new rule of the Mashiah.

00:22:08.939 --> 00:22:12.739
Therefore, you could have a new concept of Judaism.

00:22:12.739 --> 00:22:16.739
Judaism is no longer a political entity,

00:22:16.739 --> 00:22:19.380
as, for instance, what you see in the Sephardim was different.

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:22.859
And what you see in the Sephardim in the Middle East till today was different.

00:22:22.859 --> 00:22:26.660
Yes, we, till today, I mean, till recently.

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:30.699
I mean, till today means the days of my parents, of, you know, so on.

00:22:30.699 --> 00:22:32.339
I'll be with you in a second, all right?

00:22:32.339 --> 00:22:36.140
So, but the same thing with the Orthodox.

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:39.500
The Orthodox, Hattam Sofer, for instance,

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:42.500
who was the archenemy of Moses Mendelssohn,

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:45.459
came out with something which is, with all due respect,

00:22:45.459 --> 00:22:47.380
it's supposed to be untrue.

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:52.619
He said it is forbidden for a Jew to use arms

00:22:52.619 --> 00:22:57.260
in order to conquer Eretz Israel.

00:22:57.260 --> 00:23:00.780
Eretz Israel cannot be achieved through military means.

00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:04.900
It has to be achieved through spiritual means.

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.540
That is the policy of the Orthodox of today.

00:23:07.540 --> 00:23:09.939
That's why they feel very uncomfortable

00:23:09.939 --> 00:23:13.140
that the Mashiah, their version of Mashiah didn't come.

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:16.380
The Mashiah that will come is a military Mashiah.

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:20.780
You don't like Moshe Dayan, but Moshe Dayan and Sharon

00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:24.660
and all these people, those are the people who fought and brought it.

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:26.060
And they deal with this.

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:28.939
By the way, the Sephardim were to see, the Hakhamim, the Sephardim,

00:23:28.939 --> 00:23:31.500
they were immediately, they came out against that,

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:33.939
said, no, we're not going to do it with arms.

00:23:33.939 --> 00:23:37.579
So, in a sense, that's what I wanted to bring to your attention,

00:23:37.579 --> 00:23:39.459
I'll be with you in a second, Elliot,

00:23:39.459 --> 00:23:47.060
the ideas of Shabbat el-Seviyeh transformed the Jewish world.

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:48.339
How?

00:23:48.339 --> 00:23:52.979
Number one, with our religion, we're no longer a nation.

00:23:52.979 --> 00:23:55.060
Number two, because of this ideology,

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:59.979
we could join today into the Goy establishment.

00:23:59.979 --> 00:24:05.900
We could become Goy citizens, citizens of a Goy country, all right?

00:24:05.900 --> 00:24:10.300
And if we become citizens of a Goy country,

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:15.420
then the whole notion of Mashiah cannot be like Rambam.

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:20.219
It has to be, I don't mean to be disrespectful,

00:24:20.219 --> 00:24:22.219
but a kind of a Jesus kind of a Mashiah.

00:24:22.219 --> 00:24:24.459
Not this way, he's going to do it this way, you know,

00:24:24.459 --> 00:24:26.900
but it's basically like this, he's going to be flying in the air

00:24:26.900 --> 00:24:30.619
and he's going to change something, the Kuvah el-Lamod, and so on.

00:24:30.619 --> 00:24:41.380
That is one of the facts that came out of this Shabbat el-Seviyeh movement, all right?

00:24:41.380 --> 00:24:42.819
Elliot, and then I'm going to proceed.

00:24:42.819 --> 00:24:46.500
In terms of dates, Shabbat el-Seviyeh...

00:24:46.500 --> 00:24:53.099
Shabbat el-Seviyeh, very simple, Shabbat el-Seviyeh died 1676.

00:24:53.099 --> 00:24:54.099
And Napoleon?

00:24:54.099 --> 00:24:57.459
And Napoleon, it came a hundred years later.

00:24:57.459 --> 00:25:01.579
Yeah, but don't forget that even after Shabbat el-Seviyeh, as I explained to you,

00:25:01.579 --> 00:25:05.339
there was a whole movement after this that they saw him, Gilgul, not Gilgul,

00:25:05.339 --> 00:25:07.339
resurrected like Elvis Presley.

00:25:07.339 --> 00:25:11.219
He used to see Shabbat el-Seviyeh all over, you know, like this, all right?

00:25:11.219 --> 00:25:17.380
So, he didn't just die in that way, he continued, yes.

00:25:17.380 --> 00:25:22.260
And then you have, you know, so that was the...

00:25:22.260 --> 00:25:29.380
It took a hundred years, but a hundred years in history, it is not too much, you know?

00:25:29.380 --> 00:25:33.339
And the Jews were looking for alternatives, all right?

00:25:33.339 --> 00:25:34.339
Yes, sir?

00:25:34.339 --> 00:25:40.660
We're citizens of Italy, of France, and so what's the difference?

00:25:40.660 --> 00:25:43.579
It's not different, it's not different.

00:25:43.579 --> 00:25:46.819
Back home in Egypt, we were not Egyptians, we were not...

00:25:46.819 --> 00:25:50.540
Exactly, also we were not citizens.

00:25:50.699 --> 00:25:52.699
We were, we were, we were...

00:25:52.699 --> 00:25:57.819
Now, one thing that is, I believe that the Ashkenaz historians

00:25:57.819 --> 00:26:01.979
have misinterpreted the things that they always speak about the Jew in Muslim country

00:26:01.979 --> 00:26:03.979
as being a second-rate citizen.

00:26:03.979 --> 00:26:06.380
We were not a second-rate citizen.

00:26:06.380 --> 00:26:11.140
We were citizens of the Jewish Taifei,

00:26:11.140 --> 00:26:16.180
Jewish Taifei, or Sheheb, or whatever it is,

00:26:16.180 --> 00:26:19.060
Israel, or Yehudi.

00:26:19.060 --> 00:26:23.579
They used to call it Abrani, or Musawi, or whatever the word was.

00:26:23.579 --> 00:26:29.020
But you were formally recognized as a foreign citizen,

00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:34.900
and that is why they could expel you,

00:26:34.900 --> 00:26:38.260
because you are basically a foreign citizen.

00:26:38.260 --> 00:26:43.300
In my days, my days, I was not born in my days, of my father,

00:26:43.300 --> 00:26:44.979
Jews did not serve in the army.

00:26:44.979 --> 00:26:46.339
How was it? Did they serve in the army?

00:26:46.339 --> 00:26:47.819
They did not serve in the army.

00:26:47.819 --> 00:26:48.540
There it is.

00:26:48.540 --> 00:26:52.099
They did not serve in the army because we were foreign.

00:26:52.099 --> 00:26:56.180
That is, when the Sepharadi Jews came to America,

00:26:56.180 --> 00:26:58.180
and I was talking with Peter Stuyvesant,

00:26:58.180 --> 00:27:00.180
they say he was anti-Semite.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:02.500
Peter Stuyvesant may have been anti-Semite,

00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:04.900
but as I point out in my things,

00:27:04.900 --> 00:27:08.459
you know what the Jews demanded when they came to America?

00:27:08.459 --> 00:27:14.260
They wanted to be recognized not as members of the Jewish religion,

00:27:14.260 --> 00:27:17.099
but of the Jewish nation.

00:27:17.099 --> 00:27:21.819
And therefore, they wanted to serve with their own platoon,

00:27:21.819 --> 00:27:24.219
to have a different platoon of Jews.

00:27:24.219 --> 00:27:27.380
There were 34 Jews, or 50 Jews, but they had their own platoon.

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:32.699
Yes, they pay taxes collectively,

00:27:32.979 --> 00:27:36.859
we don't recognize America 100%, all right?

00:27:36.859 --> 00:27:40.660
And their own educational system, their own penal system.

00:27:40.660 --> 00:27:44.979
So whatever his feelings, the feelings of Peter Stuyvesant,

00:27:44.979 --> 00:27:49.540
he cannot just guarantee issue this.

00:27:49.540 --> 00:27:56.020
He had to consult with the government in Holland, in Amsterdam, which he did.

00:27:56.020 --> 00:27:58.219
And the Dutch people, they were very nice,

00:27:58.219 --> 00:28:01.260
they extended this thing to us.

00:28:01.260 --> 00:28:06.579
By the way, when they came to the question of citizenship in this country,

00:28:06.579 --> 00:28:09.020
again, there was an issue between Sephardim and Ashkenaz,

00:28:09.020 --> 00:28:10.380
interesting issue.

00:28:10.380 --> 00:28:17.300
The point, the Rabbi at the time was Gershon Seychas Mendes.

00:28:17.300 --> 00:28:19.380
Gershon Seychas Mendes was a Rabbi of Spanish and Portuguese,

00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:21.020
was a Rabbi of Sephardim.

00:28:21.020 --> 00:28:26.579
First Jew born in America to be a Rabbi, interesting, all right?

00:28:26.579 --> 00:28:32.699
First Jew born in this country that reached the level of a Rabbi

00:28:32.699 --> 00:28:34.380
was Gershon Seychas Mendes.

00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:39.619
He was a friend and was a great supporter of George Washington.

00:28:39.619 --> 00:28:43.739
But when it came to the question of citizenship, by the way,

00:28:43.739 --> 00:28:48.780
he's one of the founders of Columbia University.

00:28:48.780 --> 00:28:53.579
He was a founder, no, from the founders.

00:28:53.579 --> 00:28:57.339
They have still a plaque at Columbia University, the founders,

00:28:57.339 --> 00:29:02.099
and he is one of the founders of Columbia University.

00:29:02.099 --> 00:29:08.500
Now, Gershon Seychas Mendes, he said an interesting thing.

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:13.579
I pointed out before, there is something wrong with our grammar, all right?

00:29:13.579 --> 00:29:17.260
Now, let me repeat again.

00:29:17.260 --> 00:29:19.339
And the thing why is wrong with the grammar,

00:29:19.339 --> 00:29:23.339
that's thank you to, shalom, Rabbi Gershon Seychas Mendes.

00:29:23.339 --> 00:29:25.619
What is the wrong with our grammar?

00:29:25.619 --> 00:29:30.140
We say Italian-American, yes?

00:29:30.140 --> 00:29:32.859
Polish-American, all right?

00:29:32.859 --> 00:29:37.780
First you mention Italian, which becomes an adjective,

00:29:37.780 --> 00:29:42.660
and then American, which is the substantive, yes?

00:29:42.660 --> 00:29:46.819
You say Polish-American.

00:29:46.819 --> 00:29:52.579
Polish is an adjective, the substantive is American.

00:29:52.579 --> 00:29:55.819
German-American.

00:29:55.819 --> 00:29:58.339
But in Jew, Italian-American, what is this?

00:29:58.339 --> 00:30:02.060
In the Jewish alphabet, it's American-Jew.

00:30:02.060 --> 00:30:03.780
What does it mean, American-Jew?

00:30:03.780 --> 00:30:09.260
The American is the adjective, the substantive thing is what?

00:30:09.260 --> 00:30:10.500
Jew.

00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:12.380
And this is what Seychas Mendes says.

00:30:12.380 --> 00:30:18.739
We should become American-Jews, never Jewish-Americans.

00:30:18.739 --> 00:30:20.939
Interesting, no?

00:30:21.459 --> 00:30:23.459
Akkar-Jewish.

00:30:27.579 --> 00:30:30.140
The adjective, what kind of a Jew?

00:30:30.140 --> 00:30:31.979
American, this.

00:30:31.979 --> 00:30:34.660
The other way is, Italian-American means,

00:30:34.660 --> 00:30:37.780
I am an American, that's the most important thing,

00:30:37.780 --> 00:30:40.660
who happens to come from Italy?

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:42.660
But he wanted to have it the other way around,

00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:44.380
and he got away with it.

00:30:44.380 --> 00:30:48.579
He says, no, we're not going to be Jewish-Americans,

00:30:48.579 --> 00:30:51.060
but American-Jews, all right?

00:30:51.060 --> 00:30:55.540
And by the way, another important thing, very important.

00:30:55.540 --> 00:30:59.339
America, and this is the answer to your question,

00:30:59.339 --> 00:31:06.140
unlike France and so on, it recognizes dual citizenship.

00:31:06.140 --> 00:31:07.660
That was from the very beginning,

00:31:07.660 --> 00:31:10.819
America recognized dual citizenship.

00:31:10.819 --> 00:31:14.060
So you could be a citizen of more than one country.

00:31:14.060 --> 00:31:15.619
Which is interesting, I'm not saying,

00:31:15.619 --> 00:31:19.140
this is not to knock off somebody from Barmenania,

00:31:19.140 --> 00:31:21.219
if I would be in the same situation of a Jew in France,

00:31:21.219 --> 00:31:22.500
I would also take a passport.

00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:26.219
I'm not going to pontificate about other Jews.

00:31:26.219 --> 00:31:29.140
But an interesting thing, from the point of view of law,

00:31:29.140 --> 00:31:33.060
because of Seychelles Mendes, being an American-Jew

00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:36.300
does not mean that I am not a citizen of another country.

00:31:36.300 --> 00:31:38.459
America, I think, is the first country in history

00:31:38.459 --> 00:31:43.060
to offer the possibility of dual citizenship.

00:31:43.060 --> 00:31:43.780
Yes, Maurice?

00:31:44.099 --> 00:31:47.260
Legally speaking, though, is there a dual citizenship?

00:31:47.260 --> 00:31:48.260
No.

00:31:48.260 --> 00:31:53.140
No, there were only up to the moment of the independence.

00:31:53.140 --> 00:31:56.619
But at least, at the point of view of theory,

00:31:56.619 --> 00:31:59.540
they recognize that we are American-Jews, not

00:31:59.540 --> 00:32:01.260
Jewish-Americans.

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:03.979
They recognize that theory, yes?

00:32:03.979 --> 00:32:07.579
Although never was, I don't think I was ever taken,

00:32:07.579 --> 00:32:10.579
I don't know if any, because America, people do not

00:32:10.579 --> 00:32:11.380
understand America.

00:32:11.380 --> 00:32:14.060
America is not Hollywood, is not what you see in the street.

00:32:14.060 --> 00:32:16.579
America is the Supreme Court.

00:32:16.579 --> 00:32:17.699
That is the real America.

00:32:17.699 --> 00:32:20.099
If you want to understand how America operates,

00:32:20.099 --> 00:32:21.300
it's the Supreme Court.

00:32:21.300 --> 00:32:24.020
I don't think that there's only this one case in the Supreme

00:32:24.020 --> 00:32:25.859
Court, I'll tell you maybe later on.

00:32:25.859 --> 00:32:29.380
There's only one case that I know where America,

00:32:29.380 --> 00:32:30.660
I'll tell you which case.

00:32:30.660 --> 00:32:33.500
All right.

00:32:33.500 --> 00:32:38.619
It happened at the beginning of the century.

00:32:38.619 --> 00:32:39.459
All right?

00:32:39.459 --> 00:32:42.699
This is the only case that I know.

00:32:42.699 --> 00:32:52.180
Now, Rhodes belonged to, at the time, was under Italy,

00:32:52.180 --> 00:32:55.180
was an Italian colony.

00:32:55.180 --> 00:32:56.459
All right?

00:32:56.459 --> 00:33:01.579
Jews from Rhodes wanted to come to America.

00:33:01.579 --> 00:33:05.780
By the way, you have in Seattle, they

00:33:05.780 --> 00:33:07.579
settled eventually in Seattle, many of them.

00:33:07.579 --> 00:33:08.500
All right?

00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:13.859
Now, when they wanted to come to America, they say, fine.

00:33:13.859 --> 00:33:19.500
But then you have your Italian, then you have to follow.

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:22.500
We have certain quota for how many Italians we allow.

00:33:22.500 --> 00:33:24.000
And therefore, since you're Italian,

00:33:24.000 --> 00:33:26.819
I have to wait another 20 years, whatever it is.

00:33:26.819 --> 00:33:32.540
There was a very famous lawyer from Los Angeles.

00:33:32.540 --> 00:33:34.619
His name is Romi.

00:33:34.619 --> 00:33:36.300
You know the family Romi?

00:33:36.300 --> 00:33:39.380
They are from, well, there's, you know Romi?

00:33:39.380 --> 00:33:41.020
Yeah.

00:33:41.020 --> 00:33:42.339
Oh, yeah, are you from Rhodes?

00:33:42.339 --> 00:33:44.739
No.

00:33:44.739 --> 00:33:47.540
Yeah, oh, you're from Egypt.

00:33:47.540 --> 00:33:48.739
Oh, I understand.

00:33:48.739 --> 00:33:49.859
So Romi.

00:33:49.859 --> 00:33:53.060
Now, he changed his name from Romi to Rome.

00:33:53.060 --> 00:33:54.420
All right?

00:33:54.420 --> 00:33:56.739
And he argued, he went to the Supreme Court,

00:33:56.739 --> 00:34:02.300
and he won, saying that the Jews, yes,

00:34:02.300 --> 00:34:04.780
even when they are citizens of another country,

00:34:04.780 --> 00:34:09.340
they still have a different legal status.

00:34:09.340 --> 00:34:13.379
And therefore, should not be considered as Italian citizens,

00:34:13.379 --> 00:34:14.979
but as Jews.

00:34:14.979 --> 00:34:17.060
And the Supreme Court of the United States

00:34:17.060 --> 00:34:19.020
recognized this claim.

00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:20.179
Very interesting.

00:34:20.179 --> 00:34:21.260
All right?

00:34:21.260 --> 00:34:26.300
So they were allowed to enter, they

00:34:26.300 --> 00:34:29.780
were not restricted by the Italian quota.

00:34:29.780 --> 00:34:33.540
So now, all right, I just wanted to present you

00:34:33.580 --> 00:34:37.939
the background.

00:34:37.939 --> 00:34:40.020
That's why it says Sephardim in the 19th century,

00:34:40.020 --> 00:34:42.020
at the beginning of the 1800s.

00:34:42.020 --> 00:34:44.060
What happened?

00:34:44.060 --> 00:34:48.780
There was, on the one hand, there was the reform movement.

00:34:48.780 --> 00:34:51.459
In the reform movement, they were gaining a lot,

00:34:51.459 --> 00:34:53.500
a lot of power, because they were

00:34:53.500 --> 00:35:00.139
able to fully participate in the political life of the states.

00:35:00.139 --> 00:35:07.340
Second, there was the Napoleon, and the Napoleon thing

00:35:07.340 --> 00:35:14.939
encouraged Jews to come forward, to become French,

00:35:14.939 --> 00:35:19.020
and participate in the French life.

00:35:19.020 --> 00:35:20.860
Then you have the other extreme.

00:35:20.860 --> 00:35:22.379
You have the orthodox.

00:35:22.379 --> 00:35:25.020
On the one hand, you say the orthodox is very nice,

00:35:25.020 --> 00:35:29.739
but they have certain kind of ideology that

00:35:29.739 --> 00:35:31.780
caused certain problems for the Sephardim.

00:35:31.780 --> 00:35:38.820
Specifically, the whole notion of anti-secular studies,

00:35:38.820 --> 00:35:42.340
anti-the study of language, of going to university,

00:35:42.340 --> 00:35:43.260
or going to this.

00:35:43.260 --> 00:35:47.020
And this also affected many Sephardim.

00:35:47.020 --> 00:35:49.419
What to do?

00:35:49.419 --> 00:35:52.540
Now, before I go further, I want to tell you

00:35:52.540 --> 00:35:54.379
something very important.

00:35:54.379 --> 00:35:56.860
The life then, from that moment on,

00:35:56.860 --> 00:36:00.100
the life of the Sephardim was separated into two parts.

00:36:00.100 --> 00:36:06.139
We lost Western, the Western Sepharadi was lost forever.

00:36:06.139 --> 00:36:07.979
What happened?

00:36:07.979 --> 00:36:09.300
People do not know.

00:36:09.300 --> 00:36:14.860
The first reform synagogue in America,

00:36:14.860 --> 00:36:17.020
you know which one is the first reform synagogue?

00:36:17.020 --> 00:36:18.500
No.

00:36:18.500 --> 00:36:22.459
Charleston, South Carolina, the Sepharadi synagogue, 1820,

00:36:22.459 --> 00:36:30.060
was the first reform synagogue in America,

00:36:30.060 --> 00:36:36.260
was that of the Sephardim in South Carolina.

00:36:36.260 --> 00:36:39.260
That means this affected us.

00:36:39.260 --> 00:36:47.860
Second, the reform synagogue in England, West End Synagogue,

00:36:47.860 --> 00:36:51.139
was founded by the brother of Montefiore.

00:36:51.139 --> 00:36:58.139
Most of the people of the reform synagogue of London,

00:36:58.139 --> 00:37:00.419
they were Sephardim.

00:37:00.419 --> 00:37:05.500
Third, the first synagogue in South America,

00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:07.300
reform synagogue in South America,

00:37:07.300 --> 00:37:11.979
was the Sepharadi synagogue in Suriname.

00:37:11.979 --> 00:37:15.300
Suriname, all right?

00:37:15.300 --> 00:37:21.340
So reform took over Sephardim in the West.

00:37:21.340 --> 00:37:25.219
That is why, from the all Sepharadi names

00:37:25.219 --> 00:37:30.540
that you find from the West, the famous Pereiras, the Mendes,

00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:33.459
this, you almost find nothing.

00:37:33.459 --> 00:37:36.419
Because all of them were, they became reformed,

00:37:36.419 --> 00:37:40.659
and eventually they totally, completely assimilated,

00:37:40.659 --> 00:37:44.300
and they became Christians.

00:37:44.300 --> 00:37:49.459
The Sephardim in the West, we lost totally, almost totally.

00:37:49.459 --> 00:37:55.860
In Italy, we preserved ourselves in Italy,

00:37:55.860 --> 00:38:03.540
in Livorno, Florence, and Venice, more or less.

00:38:03.540 --> 00:38:07.139
The rest, the Sepharadi, Milano and so on, that's late.

00:38:07.139 --> 00:38:09.899
This was the communities in Rome, Milano.

00:38:09.899 --> 00:38:13.820
Those Sephardim are from Tripoli, or from Morocco.

00:38:13.820 --> 00:38:17.780
They're not from the original settlers.

00:38:17.780 --> 00:38:20.540
Or for instance, when you go to France, you go to Avignon.

00:38:20.540 --> 00:38:22.340
You go to Avignon and see Sephardim.

00:38:22.340 --> 00:38:25.340
The Sephardim are from Morocco.

00:38:25.340 --> 00:38:29.659
Or for instance, you say in Paris, oh, Sephardim,

00:38:29.659 --> 00:38:31.379
how long have you been?

00:38:31.379 --> 00:38:34.300
The oldest that you find are from Turkey.

00:38:34.300 --> 00:38:37.060
From Turkey, 100 years ago.

00:38:37.060 --> 00:38:40.659
From Turkey, from Algiers, from Egypt,

00:38:40.659 --> 00:38:45.260
the old Sephardim totally, completely lost.

00:38:45.260 --> 00:38:46.060
We lost.

00:38:46.060 --> 00:38:50.540
The Sephardim lost the West, totally.

00:38:50.540 --> 00:38:55.780
I mean, the only place that remained in the West

00:38:55.780 --> 00:39:00.659
was Amsterdam a little bit, but then there was another place.

00:39:00.659 --> 00:39:04.739
Hazaten, they suffered in Bordeaux.

00:39:04.739 --> 00:39:09.219
Bordeaux, there were about, in the 1930s,

00:39:09.820 --> 00:39:12.060
there were like 10,000 Sepharadi Jews.

00:39:12.060 --> 00:39:13.979
But Hazaten, Bordeaux.

00:39:13.979 --> 00:39:17.060
Bordeaux is in France.

00:39:17.060 --> 00:39:19.580
No, Greece and so on, that's Turkey.

00:39:19.580 --> 00:39:21.939
That's part of the Ottoman Empire.

00:39:21.939 --> 00:39:25.379
So all those communities, most of the communities

00:39:25.379 --> 00:39:29.500
that we had in the West, they were enormous,

00:39:29.500 --> 00:39:30.979
very old communities.

00:39:30.979 --> 00:39:34.379
In the old southwest of France, we had communities.

00:39:34.379 --> 00:39:35.020
We lost them.

00:39:35.020 --> 00:39:37.659
They could become assimilated, reformed.

00:39:37.659 --> 00:39:40.020
What about the election of the Sepharadi?

00:39:40.020 --> 00:39:40.780
I don't know.

00:39:40.780 --> 00:39:44.060
I don't know, but they were into the hundreds of thousands.

00:39:44.060 --> 00:39:46.340
By the way, there were the greatest banks,

00:39:46.340 --> 00:39:49.139
the greatest banks in France and so on,

00:39:49.139 --> 00:39:50.979
they were all Sephardim.

00:39:50.979 --> 00:39:54.020
Rothschild is the first Ashkenaz to become well.

00:39:54.020 --> 00:39:55.939
But there was also the Pereiras, they

00:39:55.939 --> 00:39:58.659
were at the time as wealthy as the, still the Pereiras,

00:39:58.659 --> 00:40:01.179
they are the famous bank, Pereira and so on.

00:40:01.179 --> 00:40:04.580
There's still the Moscata in England with the gold.

00:40:04.580 --> 00:40:07.219
Still they have the Moscata brothers and so on.

00:40:07.219 --> 00:40:08.659
There's all Sephardim.

00:40:08.659 --> 00:40:11.300
All those families, most of those families,

00:40:11.300 --> 00:40:16.820
Babonotenu, they became, let me give you

00:40:16.820 --> 00:40:20.300
three examples of famous families.

00:40:20.300 --> 00:40:26.979
Benjamin Disraeli, England, become a Christian.

00:40:26.979 --> 00:40:30.500
He's prime minister of England, Sepharadi Jew.

00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.780
He's a Christian, assimilated.

00:40:32.780 --> 00:40:33.939
His father converted him.

00:40:33.939 --> 00:40:35.340
He didn't want to convert.

00:40:35.340 --> 00:40:38.419
His father converted.

00:40:38.419 --> 00:40:43.020
Now, another example, David Ricardo,

00:40:43.020 --> 00:40:46.659
the greatest, the most important economist in modern time,

00:40:46.659 --> 00:40:49.580
the founder of the Bank of England.

00:40:49.580 --> 00:40:51.139
He founded the Bank of England.

00:40:51.139 --> 00:40:54.419
That's not a joke.

00:40:54.419 --> 00:40:57.739
David Ricardo married a Christian.

00:40:57.739 --> 00:41:05.780
Isaac Pinto, who was the founder of the French Bourse,

00:41:05.780 --> 00:41:09.340
the French stock market.

00:41:09.340 --> 00:41:11.820
He did not convert and so on, but I

00:41:11.820 --> 00:41:14.500
don't know what happened to his children or grandchildren.

00:41:14.500 --> 00:41:15.260
They disappeared.

00:41:15.260 --> 00:41:17.780
I mean, they totally, totally, all those families disappeared.

00:41:17.780 --> 00:41:22.620
The Sephardim lost the West.

00:41:22.620 --> 00:41:25.419
All right, this is very important, you know.

00:41:25.419 --> 00:41:29.300
There were a few here, there, and so on, you know.

00:41:29.300 --> 00:41:31.580
We lost the West, you know.

00:41:31.580 --> 00:41:40.379
And therefore, we remain mostly Ottoman Empire, North Africa,

00:41:40.379 --> 00:41:45.580
Middle East, you know, like Iraq and those things.

00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:47.699
Let me, you raised your hand before.

00:41:47.699 --> 00:41:50.860
You're trying to be, like, after the return of the French.

00:41:50.860 --> 00:41:52.179
Yes, yes.

00:41:53.100 --> 00:41:57.260
The Jews, once after the Shabbatai Sevii movement,

00:41:57.260 --> 00:41:59.820
came two things that devastated the Jews.

00:41:59.820 --> 00:42:02.979
Either it was the possibility of reform

00:42:02.979 --> 00:42:05.739
or the possibility of becoming a citizen, yes.

00:42:05.739 --> 00:42:08.939
Now, when you go, and I don't want to shock any of you

00:42:08.939 --> 00:42:11.540
in this now, but when you go to pray

00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:16.260
in some of the synagogues, all synagogues in Europe,

00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:20.659
which are traditional, they are, like, reformed.

00:42:20.659 --> 00:42:23.260
But when you go to Rome, to the main synagogue,

00:42:23.260 --> 00:42:24.939
they play the organ.

00:42:24.939 --> 00:42:27.219
I don't know how it is in the Paris synagogue today,

00:42:27.219 --> 00:42:29.020
in the last synagogue.

00:42:29.020 --> 00:42:33.699
They have the organ, probably they do have the organ.

00:42:33.699 --> 00:42:35.699
Yes.

00:42:35.699 --> 00:42:37.899
Now, they have no more?

00:42:37.899 --> 00:42:39.739
All right, at one time, they used to have the organ.

00:42:39.739 --> 00:42:42.100
Now, maybe because there's many Moroccans, North Africans,

00:42:42.100 --> 00:42:43.020
so on, they come there.

00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:44.540
But at one time, they had the organ.

00:42:44.540 --> 00:42:47.500
They had organ, they had organ, and so on.

00:42:47.500 --> 00:42:50.659
And some of them, they're very, very difficult

00:42:50.659 --> 00:42:54.419
to distinguish between them and reform,

00:42:54.419 --> 00:43:01.939
because I just wanted to know that we lost the West.

00:43:01.939 --> 00:43:08.979
All right, now, what to do?

00:43:08.979 --> 00:43:10.139
What to do?

00:43:10.139 --> 00:43:14.979
That is the crisis, the paradigm in the 19th century.

00:43:14.979 --> 00:43:16.419
What I'm going to tell you is one

00:43:16.419 --> 00:43:21.219
of the most brilliant chapters in our history.

00:43:21.219 --> 00:43:23.739
Unfortunately, it's unknown.

00:43:23.739 --> 00:43:27.500
I've written about it enormously for the last 20, 30 years.

00:43:27.500 --> 00:43:29.379
And although I've written about it,

00:43:29.379 --> 00:43:32.580
and some Ashkenaz already are acknowledging the points,

00:43:32.580 --> 00:43:34.340
of course, without mentioning me.

00:43:34.340 --> 00:43:39.939
But the truth is that we, Sephardim,

00:43:39.939 --> 00:43:43.500
are not aware of what happened at the beginning

00:43:43.500 --> 00:43:47.939
of the 19th century.

00:43:47.939 --> 00:43:53.379
The most important man was Rabbi Yisrael Moshe Hazzan.

00:43:53.379 --> 00:43:55.540
Tell me a little about Moshe Hazzan.

00:43:55.540 --> 00:43:58.340
Moshe Hazzan, the Hazzan family, was

00:43:58.340 --> 00:44:04.100
the most prestigious rabbinic family known in this.

00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:06.500
Great-grandparents for generations

00:44:06.500 --> 00:44:09.419
that had been chief rabbis of Israel.

00:44:09.419 --> 00:44:12.540
Eliyahu Hazzan was the chief Rabbi of Cairo.

00:44:15.540 --> 00:44:19.340
Yosef Hazzan was the chief Rabbi, first, of Izmir,

00:44:19.340 --> 00:44:25.659
then of Istanbul, then of Erez Israel, Rishon Lesion.

00:44:25.659 --> 00:44:29.659
The cousin of Rabbi Yisrael Moshe Hazzan was Rabbi Haim Palache.

00:44:29.659 --> 00:44:33.580
He was one of the most prestigious rabbis.

00:44:33.580 --> 00:44:38.179
When he was a young man, Yisrael Moshe Hazzan

00:44:38.179 --> 00:44:46.620
is sent as a shaliah from Erez Israel to Western Europe

00:44:46.620 --> 00:44:48.659
to raise money.

00:44:48.659 --> 00:44:52.620
Now, the institution of the shalihut

00:44:52.620 --> 00:44:56.739
was one of the oldest and most important institutions

00:44:56.739 --> 00:44:58.500
in the Sepharadi world.

00:44:58.500 --> 00:45:01.459
What this institution consisted of?

00:45:01.459 --> 00:45:06.699
Jews from all over the Sepharadi world, from the Americas,

00:45:06.699 --> 00:45:11.699
used to come to places like Barbados, Curaçao, Suriname,

00:45:11.699 --> 00:45:18.379
New York, Philadelphia, to places as far as Goa in India.

00:45:18.379 --> 00:45:22.179
The shalihim would come and raise money

00:45:22.179 --> 00:45:28.100
for the four main yeshivot of the Sephardim, which

00:45:28.100 --> 00:45:34.620
were in Jerusalem, Safed, Hebron.

00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:40.899
That's right, Hebron, Jerusalem, Safed, and what else?

00:45:40.899 --> 00:45:42.500
And Tiberia.

00:45:42.500 --> 00:45:43.000
That's it.

00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:44.699
That's the four places.

00:45:44.699 --> 00:45:48.739
Now, Jews from all over the world would contribute.

00:45:48.739 --> 00:45:52.699
And therefore, these four cities, Tiberia, Hebron,

00:45:52.699 --> 00:45:59.100
Jerusalem, Safed, were like the universities of the Jews,

00:45:59.100 --> 00:46:02.459
whom they used to send as a shaliah.

00:46:02.459 --> 00:46:06.300
The people they sent as a shaliah was the best that we had,

00:46:06.300 --> 00:46:10.100
people who eventually will become the chief rabbis of Israel.

00:46:10.100 --> 00:46:15.060
And the shaliah, the shalihut, lasted for years and years.

00:46:15.060 --> 00:46:20.340
Yisrael Moshe Hazzan, as a young man in his early 20s, 23,

00:46:20.340 --> 00:46:23.139
he is sent to Europe.

00:46:23.139 --> 00:46:30.540
And he goes and he visits places like Prague in Czechoslovakia,

00:46:30.540 --> 00:46:33.459
Rome.

00:46:33.459 --> 00:46:36.699
He goes to Amsterdam.

00:46:36.699 --> 00:46:40.500
He goes to England.

00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:47.820
And for the first time, he sees what is going on in the world.

00:46:47.820 --> 00:46:52.820
He discovers both the danger of the reform movement.

00:46:56.419 --> 00:46:59.620
I want to read for you some of the things that he wrote.

00:47:00.060 --> 00:47:01.699
It's so amazing.

00:47:01.699 --> 00:47:05.179
It's so amazing that it simply escapes the mind

00:47:05.179 --> 00:47:14.580
how a person so many years ago would have been able to,

00:47:14.580 --> 00:47:25.060
you know, he says like this, he says, he says like this.

00:47:25.060 --> 00:47:33.179
He says, behold, there it lays before us,

00:47:33.179 --> 00:47:39.699
the great corruption that prevails among us in Europe,

00:47:39.699 --> 00:47:45.179
